<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Brienne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Brienne was a French noble family from Brienne-le-Château in Champagne that rose to prominence in the crusader states. John of Brienne became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1210 and later co-emperor of the Latin Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, his nephew Walter IV was Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, and Walter V became Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in 1308 before being killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalan Company</a> in 1311. The family's heirs kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-brienne.jpg" alt="House of Brienne" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA (talk · contribs). See sourced file for original authors. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_Brienne_(Counts_of_Brienne).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
